# Flotta — LOCAL dev settings.
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # .env is gitignored; never commit real values
#
# Loaded automatically by the justfile (`set dotenv-load := true`), so every
# `just` recipe sees these. Note that `just` loads a file named exactly `.env`
# — a `.env.local` is NOT read.
#
# Two groups below: settings that configure YOUR MACHINE, and provider
# credentials that are pushed to a box as Fly secrets (`just fly-secrets`).

# --- Authentication (M5) ---------------------------------------------------

# The key every scoped token is signed with. Generate one with:
#
#   flotta token key
#
# The SAME value must be set wherever the control plane runs, or tokens minted
# here will not verify there. Rotating it revokes every token at once — which
# is how revocation works, so keep token lifetimes short.
#
# Unset means the control plane runs UNAUTHENTICATED, which it will only do on
# a loopback bind. A public bind with no key is refused at startup.
#FLOTTA_SIGNING_KEY=

# The dashboard's own token. Read-only is the right scope for a fleet view:
#
#   flotta token mint dashboard --scope fleet:read
#
# Add --scope box:destroy only if the kill button should work, i.e. if anyone
# with dashboard access may delete an agent's entire memory.
#FLOTTA_CONTROL_TOKEN=

# How long a box may sit with no live task and no activity before it is
# suspended. Default 1800 (30 minutes). Set 0 to disable, for anyone who would
# rather pay for a warm box than wait 10-60s for it to wake.
#FLOTTA_IDLE_AFTER_S=1800

# --- Fly credentials for the control plane ---------------------------------

# Only needed where the CONTROL PLANE runs, not on your laptop — locally the
# CLI uses your own `flyctl auth login`. A deployed control plane has no
# interactive login, so it needs a token: `flyctl tokens create org`.
#
# Without it the deployed control plane serves reads and nothing else:
# creating, waking, destroying and suspending a box all go through flyctl.
#FLY_API_TOKEN=

# --- the front door (M5b) --------------------------------------------------

# Where the control plane is reachable. The door asks it which machine a box is
# and to wake it, so this must be the PUBLIC url, not localhost.
#FLOTTA_CONTROL_URL=https://<your-app>.up.railway.app

# The domain boxes are addressed under: <box>.$FLOTTA_DOMAIN
#FLOTTA_DOMAIN=flotta.dev

# The domain boxes sign commits under: <box>@$FLOTTA_GIT_EMAIL_DOMAIN.
# Defaults to $FLOTTA_DOMAIN, and to `boxes.invalid` when there is no domain at
# all — an RFC 2606 / RFC 6761 reserved TLD, so the address can never be
# verified on a GitHub account and can never be linked to a person. Set this
# only to move commits onto a domain you own; `just box-identity` carries
# whichever of the two is set onto the machine.
#FLOTTA_GIT_EMAIL_DOMAIN=agents.example.com

# The door's Fly app. Fly app names are globally unique across all of Fly, not
# per-org, so the default may already be taken by somebody else.
#FLOTTA_DOOR_APP=flotta-door

# --- Fly target (M2: the box tier) -----------------------------------------

# Which Fly org, app and volume every `just fly-*` recipe acts on. Pinned for
# a reason with precedent: flyctl acts on whichever org happens to be current,
# and back when this repo used Modal its globally-active profile was once found
# pointing at an unrelated workspace. `just fly-whoami` prints the
# resolved target and gates every other fly recipe.
#
# Log in first (this is yours to run — it opens a browser):
#
#   fly auth login
#   fly orgs list          # the SLUG column is what goes below
#
# `personal` exists on every Fly account and is the default.
#FLOTTA_FLY_ORG=personal

# Fly app names are **globally unique across all of Fly**, not per-org, so the
# default `flotta-box` is almost certainly taken. Pick your own.
#FLOTTA_FLY_APP=flotta-box-yourname

# Leave unset and the nearest region is *detected* — every Fly edge echoes the
# region that served a request in a `Fly-Region` header, so one unauthenticated
# request answers "where is nearest?". Fly itself does not get a say: `fly
# volumes create` refuses to run without an explicit region when it is not
# attached to a TTY, so something has to name one before the disk exists.
# `just fly-whoami` prints what will be used.
#FLOTTA_FLY_REGION=ams

# The disk that makes a box a box. Volumes bill whether the machine is running,
# stopped or suspended (~$0.15/GB/month), so a stopped box is cheap, not free.
# 1GB is plenty for state.db + memories + skills.
#FLOTTA_FLY_VOLUME_NAME=flotta_data
#FLOTTA_FLY_VOLUME_GB=1

# --- Provider credentials (pushed to a box) --------------------------------
#
# Read by the agent on a box, but indirectly: `just fly-secrets` pushes them
# into Fly secrets and the machine reads them from its environment, so a key is
# never baked into the image.
#
# After changing any value here, run `just fly-secrets`. No rebuild is needed,
# but it is not instant: Fly secrets become environment variables when a
# machine *starts*, so a running box serves the old value until you
# `flotta stop <box>` and `flotta start <box>`.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works. Hermes's own default is OpenRouter;
# swap the base URL and model for OpenAI, Nous Portal, a local vLLM, etc.
#
# Needed only for `just e2e-live` and non-dry-run spawns.
#
#FLOTTA_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4
#FLOTTA_MODEL_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#FLOTTA_API_KEY=sk-or-...

# --- Cost estimation (optional) --------------------------------------------
#
# Dollars per container-second, used to fill the `cost_estimate` column the CLI
# and dashboard show. **Unset by default**, and then every surface renders an
# em dash rather than a number.
#
# Why you have to supply this: a substrate's billing API attributes cost to an
# app or an org over a day, not to one task. The estimate is therefore duration
# x a rate *you* choose, and a rate nobody chose would be a fabricated number
# that looks authoritative.
#
# Covers machine time only. Model tokens are a separate bill Flotta never sees,
# and so is volume storage — a stopped box is cheap, not free.
#
#FLOTTA_COST_PER_SECOND=0.0000131

# OPENAI_BASE_URL / OPENAI_API_KEY are honoured as fallbacks for the two above,
# so an existing OpenAI-style environment works without renaming anything.

# --- Worker runtime (NOT set here) -----------------------------------------
#
# The remaining worker variables are per-spawn, not per-machine: the spawner
# passes them into each container, so setting them here has no effect.
#
#   FLOTTA_TASK        the task prompt          (set by spawn_worker)
#   FLOTTA_TIMEOUT_S   hard task timeout, 900s  (spawn_worker's timeout_s)
#   FLOTTA_ONESHOT     run-once vs. serve mode
#   FLOTTA_HOST/PORT   MCP bind address         (never 3000 — reserved)
#   FLOTTA_AUTH_TOKEN  bearer token for the worker's MCP endpoint
#   FLOTTA_TOOLSETS    CSV of Hermes toolsets   (unset = Hermes default)
#   HERMES_HOME        Hermes store. /tmp/hermes on a Tier 3 worker (ephemeral
#                      by design); /data/hermes on a box, inside the mounted
#                      volume — that relocation is what M2 is about.
#
# The authoritative table is the module docstring of:
#
#   src/flotta/worker/config.py
